1
00:00:00,967 --> 00:00:02,433
<i> What are you doing to Joey?</i>

2
00:00:02,567 --> 00:00:03,433
<i> You misunderstood it.</i>

3
00:00:03,567 --> 00:00:04,533
<i> I have no problem.</i>

4
00:00:04,667 --> 00:00:06,000
<i> Is it true, Joey?</i>

5
00:00:06,133 --> 00:00:07,000
<i> What happened last night?</i>

6
00:00:07,133 --> 00:00:08,500
<i> I blacked out.</i>

7
00:00:08,633 --> 00:00:10,867
<i>Don't you remember
what I said to you?</i>

8
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:14,000
<i>Even though we are different,
I love you.</i>

9
00:00:14,133 --> 00:00:15,367
<i> What did you say?</i>

10
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:17,733
<i>So, even what you said to me
last night,</i>

11
00:00:17,867 --> 00:00:18,867
<i> you don't remember?</i>

12
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:22,733
<i>- You're perfect, handsome.
- Am I handsome?</i>

13
00:00:22,867 --> 00:00:23,800
<i> I don't remember anything.</i>

14
00:00:23,933 --> 00:00:24,767
<i> What did I say?</i>

15
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:25,933
<i> I've talked to Trigger.</i>

16
00:00:26,067 --> 00:00:26,933
<i> He agreed to what you wanted.</i>

17
00:00:27,067 --> 00:00:28,267
<i> I just want to know.</i>

18
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:29,567
<i> What if you betray me</i>

19
00:00:29,700 --> 00:00:32,300
<i>like what you did to your best
friend, Major Aglipay?</i>

20
00:00:32,433 --> 00:00:33,433
<i> He betrayed me.</i>

21
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:35,200
<i>I'm not part of their syndicate.</i>

22
00:00:35,333 --> 00:00:37,167
<i> Hey, what are you doing there?</i>

23
00:00:37,300 --> 00:00:38,233
<i> You're in luck now.</i>

24
00:00:38,367 --> 00:00:39,767
<i>I've already spoken
to my husband</i>

25
00:00:39,900 --> 00:00:41,833
<i> about your husband's case.</i>

26
00:00:41,967 --> 00:00:44,167
<i>When he arrives,
I'll introduce you to him.</i>

27
00:00:44,300 --> 00:00:47,033
<i> An invitation has arrived
from one of our target sponsors.</i>

28
00:00:47,167 --> 00:00:48,500
<i> Confirm my attendance.</i>

29
00:00:48,633 --> 00:00:52,567
<i>I'll try to get access to their
office and find the guest list.</i>

30
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:54,633
<i>Just make sure that my name
is on that list.</i>

31
00:00:54,767 --> 00:00:56,267
<i>Didn't we already talk
about this, Joey?</i>

32
00:00:56,400 --> 00:00:57,167
<i> You're not coming.</i>

33
00:00:57,300 --> 00:00:59,400
<i>Please, Andrew, I can fight too.</i>

34
00:00:59,533 --> 00:01:00,700
<i> You're so weak.</i>

35
00:01:00,833 --> 00:01:02,533
<i> Okay, I'll beat you.</i>

36
00:01:02,667 --> 00:01:03,467
<i> I got you.</i>

37
00:01:03,600 --> 00:01:04,633
<i> Are you sure?</i>

38
00:01:04,767 --> 00:01:07,733
<i>Joey, can being a black
belter help you here?</i>

39
00:01:07,900 --> 00:01:11,067
<i>Remember, your opponents
are gun smugglers.</i>

40
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:13,067
<i> It's my hair.</i>

41
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:14,233
<i> It's always good to be ready.</i>

42
00:01:14,367 --> 00:01:16,267
<i>It's even better if you hit it.</i>

43
00:01:16,400 --> 00:01:19,200
<i> Keep aiming after every shot.</i>

44
00:01:47,633 --> 00:01:49,267
Joey, Joey.

45
00:01:50,867 --> 00:01:52,767
Can we talk?

46
00:01:56,533 --> 00:01:59,467
Are you looking for Peter?

47
00:02:01,233 --> 00:02:07,000
He and Jin Ho have left
to get the guest list.

48
00:02:09,767 --> 00:02:11,267
I wanted to apologize.

49
00:02:15,133 --> 00:02:16,600
Oh, wait...

50
00:02:17,633 --> 00:02:18,300
Are you okay?

51
00:02:18,433 --> 00:02:19,700
Do you have a fever?

52
00:02:21,467 --> 00:02:22,233
No.

53
00:02:23,333 --> 00:02:24,200
Ah...

54
00:02:25,067 --> 00:02:27,433
I thought so, well, you were
going to apologize.

55
00:02:28,733 --> 00:02:30,133
Joey, I'm serious.

56
00:02:32,167 --> 00:02:36,000
I really want to apologize
for lying to you.

57
00:02:36,833 --> 00:02:38,100
I'm not really looking down
on you

58
00:02:38,233 --> 00:02:41,667
because you're a woman,

59
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:45,300
and I don't think
you're a failure.

60
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:50,967
I know that, that's why
I don't understand you.

61
00:02:52,700 --> 00:02:53,900
We're all here

62
00:02:54,033 --> 00:02:56,933
because we're helping each other
find Golda,

63
00:02:57,067 --> 00:02:58,900
and you're going
to tell me that.

64
00:03:00,167 --> 00:03:02,367
You know, it's hard to
be vulnerable with you.

65
00:03:03,133 --> 00:03:04,633
You're such a big scammer.

66
00:03:05,933 --> 00:03:07,167
Ah, yes.

67
00:03:10,800 --> 00:03:13,000
I hope you know
that I only did that

68
00:03:13,133 --> 00:03:18,200
because your father asked me
to watch over you.

69
00:03:19,700 --> 00:03:20,600
Father?

70
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:22,200
Yup...

71
00:03:22,333 --> 00:03:23,800
When I visited him,

72
00:03:23,933 --> 00:03:27,133
I told him about our mission
here,

73
00:03:27,267 --> 00:03:30,067
and he was super worried
about you

74
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:34,733
because we both know that you
only get more stubborn

75
00:03:34,867 --> 00:03:37,700
when someone is trying
to stop you,

76
00:03:37,833 --> 00:03:41,000
especially if what you're doing
is for him.

77
00:03:42,033 --> 00:03:43,000
There you go.

78
00:03:43,133 --> 00:03:46,100
Well, I wish you had just
said that right away

79
00:03:46,233 --> 00:03:47,633
because I could have taken it
better

80
00:03:47,767 --> 00:03:49,800
than those brutal things
you said.

81
00:03:53,700 --> 00:04:03,367
Okay, I'm sorry, but I only said
that so you can be angry with me

82
00:04:03,533 --> 00:04:07,100
and not think that your father
doesn't trust you.

83
00:04:10,733 --> 00:04:12,167
I understand that.

84
00:04:16,333 --> 00:04:19,967
I'm also sorry
because I lied to you.

85
00:04:22,100 --> 00:04:24,333
I lied that I could do it alone.

86
00:04:26,267 --> 00:04:30,267
But the truth is, I still need
my three musketeers.

87
00:04:30,433 --> 00:04:31,500
I still need you.

88
00:04:35,133 --> 00:04:35,967
I thought it was just me.

89
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:38,033
When did I say that?

90
00:04:40,033 --> 00:04:41,533
That's why "I thought".

91
00:04:41,667 --> 00:04:43,200
You're assuming.

92
00:04:48,800 --> 00:04:50,667
Hey, compadre!

93
00:04:50,800 --> 00:04:53,767
Oh, it's just a small party.

94
00:04:53,900 --> 00:04:56,100
Yes, you shouldn't miss it, huh?

95
00:04:57,433 --> 00:04:58,967
Yes, yes, it's my birthday,

96
00:04:59,100 --> 00:05:01,800
but we'll still talk business,
okay?

97
00:05:01,967 --> 00:05:03,033
See you there, compadre.

98
00:05:03,167 --> 00:05:04,033
Goodbye.

99
00:05:05,033 --> 00:05:06,133
Hi, Godfather.

100
00:05:06,267 --> 00:05:07,500
Golda.

101
00:05:07,633 --> 00:05:08,967
I have a gift for you.

102
00:05:09,100 --> 00:05:12,000
Oh, you shouldn't have bothered,
but what is it?

103
00:05:12,133 --> 00:05:12,833
Take a look.

104
00:05:15,667 --> 00:05:17,800
Braganza is coming!

105
00:05:17,933 --> 00:05:20,367
Happy birthday, Godfather.

106
00:05:20,500 --> 00:05:21,567
Thank you, Golda.

107
00:05:22,267 --> 00:05:25,500
If he talks sensibly,
we won't have any problems.

108
00:05:26,300 --> 00:05:27,467
Hey, Godfather.

109
00:05:27,600 --> 00:05:31,667
When this deal goes through,
this won't be your best gift.

110
00:05:32,300 --> 00:05:36,200
This will be the biggest
and most bonggacious deal

111
00:05:36,367 --> 00:05:38,433
in the nation!

112
00:05:38,567 --> 00:05:39,467
Bonggacious?

113
00:05:39,600 --> 00:05:43,133
Yeah, bonggacious like you,
like us!

114
00:05:43,267 --> 00:05:45,433
You're such a sweet talker.

115
00:05:45,567 --> 00:05:47,733
I'm so excited for this deal,
Godfather.

116
00:05:47,867 --> 00:05:49,033
I hope it pushes through.

117
00:05:49,167 --> 00:05:51,633
Yes, it will, it will.

118
00:05:55,967 --> 00:05:57,667
Yes, a little, Joey.

119
00:05:57,800 --> 00:05:58,533
As in stressed.

120
00:05:58,667 --> 00:06:00,167
I'm that busy.

121
00:06:00,300 --> 00:06:02,167
Oh, why, Mother?

122
00:06:02,300 --> 00:06:05,233
My boss is taking me to a party,

123
00:06:05,367 --> 00:06:08,133
so I need to finish
what I'm doing first.

124
00:06:08,300 --> 00:06:10,733
Your boss is taking you?

125
00:06:10,867 --> 00:06:14,000
You seem close, Mother.

126
00:06:14,133 --> 00:06:15,100
<i> A little.</i>

127
00:06:15,233 --> 00:06:16,600
I hope so.

128
00:06:16,733 --> 00:06:20,167
You know, Joey,
they're really nice.

129
00:06:20,300 --> 00:06:21,267
<i> Do you know?</i>

130
00:06:21,400 --> 00:06:24,200
<i>Next week, she'll make me
talk to her husband.</i>

131
00:06:24,333 --> 00:06:25,800
Let's see if there's anything
he can do

132
00:06:25,933 --> 00:06:27,633
to help your father's case.

133
00:06:27,767 --> 00:06:29,400
Really?

134
00:06:29,533 --> 00:06:31,767
Oh my, they seem kind, Mother.

135
00:06:31,900 --> 00:06:33,700
How about you Joey,
are you going somewhere?

136
00:06:43,033 --> 00:06:44,533
Joey?

137
00:06:44,667 --> 00:06:45,300
Ah, no, Mother.

138
00:06:45,433 --> 00:06:47,167
I'll see first.

139
00:06:47,300 --> 00:06:48,767
Okay...

140
00:06:48,900 --> 00:06:49,333
Love you, Mother.

141
00:06:49,467 --> 00:06:50,267
<i> Okay.</i>

142
00:06:55,833 --> 00:06:56,633
Do it again.

143
00:06:57,500 --> 00:06:58,167
How?

144
00:07:01,267 --> 00:07:02,033
What's that?

145
00:07:05,367 --> 00:07:07,800
Do you know? We had a lot of
trouble getting that invitation.

146
00:07:08,933 --> 00:07:10,200
That's why we just arrived,

147
00:07:10,333 --> 00:07:12,467
we still had to look
for a target.

148
00:07:12,600 --> 00:07:14,367
Catalina Esperanza.

149
00:07:15,933 --> 00:07:16,533
That would be you.

150
00:07:17,567 --> 00:07:19,233
The theme is The Great Gatsby.

151
00:07:19,367 --> 00:07:20,333
How about that?

152
00:07:20,467 --> 00:07:21,300
I won't wear anything.

153
00:07:21,433 --> 00:07:22,567
We didn't prepare.

154
00:07:22,700 --> 00:07:23,767
Costume?

155
00:07:23,900 --> 00:07:24,300
Wait.

156
00:07:29,200 --> 00:07:30,333
Confirmed, Boss.

157
00:07:30,467 --> 00:07:32,367
Braganza already has a target
here in Luzon.

158
00:07:33,233 --> 00:07:34,567
<i> Who?</i>

159
00:07:34,700 --> 00:07:35,567
Godfather.

160
00:07:35,700 --> 00:07:37,900
They seem to be
planning something.

161
00:07:38,033 --> 00:07:39,567
Alcala?

162
00:07:39,700 --> 00:07:41,800
He's a gun smuggler.

163
00:07:41,933 --> 00:07:45,933
<i>What does Braganza have to do
with him being a drug dealer?</i>

164
00:07:46,067 --> 00:07:48,567
We need to find out what
they're up to, Matias.

165
00:07:48,733 --> 00:07:50,700
<i>There's a party going
on at Godfather's.</i>

166
00:07:50,833 --> 00:07:53,067
It looks like the transaction
will happen there.

167
00:07:53,200 --> 00:07:54,233
Then we need to get in.

168
00:07:56,967 --> 00:08:00,033
Are you talking about
Godfather's 65th birthday bash?

169
00:08:01,400 --> 00:08:02,733
Guess who got an invite.

170
00:08:05,767 --> 00:08:06,533
Don't worry.

171
00:08:07,533 --> 00:08:08,567
<i> I'll take care of it.</i>

172
00:08:15,433 --> 00:08:16,767
Joey, you're taking too long!

173
00:08:16,900 --> 00:08:17,900
Let's go!

174
00:08:19,100 --> 00:08:20,567
Joey!

175
00:08:20,700 --> 00:08:21,900
Coming, wait a minute.

176
00:08:23,933 --> 00:08:24,600
There you go...

177
00:08:24,733 --> 00:08:25,333
There you go,
there you go.

178
00:08:25,467 --> 00:08:26,033
There you go. Almost there.

179
00:08:55,467 --> 00:08:56,300
Isn't it too tight?

180
00:08:57,300 --> 00:08:58,167
Is it okay?

181
00:09:13,900 --> 00:09:14,967
Why? Is it ugly?

182
00:09:16,033 --> 00:09:17,667
Peter, is it ugly?

183
00:09:21,400 --> 00:09:22,133
It's not.

184
00:09:23,567 --> 00:09:24,267
It's just right.

185
00:09:25,500 --> 00:09:26,300
That will do.

186
00:09:27,933 --> 00:09:29,667
Wait, it's hot.

187
00:09:29,800 --> 00:09:30,767
Let me get some water first,
okay?

188
00:09:30,900 --> 00:09:31,900
It's hot.

189
00:09:32,033 --> 00:09:33,433
Sorry.

190
00:09:33,567 --> 00:09:34,400
What's his problem?

191
00:09:36,167 --> 00:09:37,133
Andrew, is it okay, right?

192
00:09:37,267 --> 00:09:38,300
Or is it too tight?

193
00:09:40,100 --> 00:09:40,900
Ah...

194
00:09:43,433 --> 00:09:47,533
Well, I don't know about that,
I don't wear that.

195
00:09:48,567 --> 00:09:49,700
Right?

196
00:09:49,833 --> 00:09:50,667
Anyway...

197
00:09:52,467 --> 00:09:53,267
I'll go outside first.

198
00:09:58,333 --> 00:09:59,867
Oh, it's hard
to talk to them.

199
00:10:01,733 --> 00:10:03,633
Is it ugly?

200
00:10:03,767 --> 00:10:05,067
Jin Ho, it's okay, right?

201
00:10:07,433 --> 00:10:08,233
What?

202
00:10:09,467 --> 00:10:10,300
It's okay, right?

203
00:10:10,433 --> 00:10:11,367
I'm not thinking about you.

204
00:10:15,567 --> 00:10:16,333
Excuse me.

205
00:10:17,367 --> 00:10:18,200
Oh...

206
00:10:21,467 --> 00:10:22,100
Is it ugly?

207
00:10:22,233 --> 00:10:23,800
I don't look like a rice cake.

208
00:10:31,067 --> 00:10:33,400
Oh, Ma'am, the proposal
is ready...

209
00:10:33,533 --> 00:10:34,333
Okay.

210
00:10:34,500 --> 00:10:36,767
The one you asked me to print.

211
00:10:36,900 --> 00:10:38,133
Oh, wait, we can do that later.

212
00:10:38,267 --> 00:10:39,133
Let me look at you.

213
00:10:41,533 --> 00:10:42,367
Wow!

214
00:10:43,667 --> 00:10:44,800
Thank you very much.

215
00:10:47,167 --> 00:10:49,033
Thank you for the costume
you lent me.

216
00:10:50,133 --> 00:10:52,367
You too, you look so elegant.

217
00:10:53,100 --> 00:10:56,033
You know, we should do this
more often.

218
00:10:56,167 --> 00:10:59,933
We should dress up,
and we should go out,

219
00:11:00,067 --> 00:11:02,700
not when it's just someone's
birthday.

220
00:11:02,833 --> 00:11:05,300
Oh, Ma'am, you can do that.

221
00:11:06,200 --> 00:11:07,667
But me, with so much in my head,

222
00:11:07,800 --> 00:11:09,267
and I have to take care
of a lot of things,

223
00:11:09,433 --> 00:11:11,533
I can't do it anymore.

224
00:11:12,767 --> 00:11:16,633
Which is why you deserve
nights like this.

225
00:11:16,767 --> 00:11:18,300
You know, you work hard.

226
00:11:18,433 --> 00:11:20,233
You carry so much.

227
00:11:20,367 --> 00:11:23,867
Even joy needs to be
scheduled sometimes.

228
00:11:25,267 --> 00:11:27,733
Come on. Turn around again,
turn around.

229
00:11:31,900 --> 00:11:33,600
The costume is beautiful.

230
00:11:33,733 --> 00:11:36,500
But it seems like
something is missing.

231
00:11:37,500 --> 00:11:38,367
Is it still not enough?

232
00:11:38,500 --> 00:11:40,800
Well, I'm already shiny.

233
00:11:40,933 --> 00:11:42,300
Come on.

234
00:11:42,467 --> 00:11:43,300
Hold on.

235
00:11:46,233 --> 00:11:47,533
There you go!

236
00:11:47,667 --> 00:11:48,667
Here.

237
00:11:48,800 --> 00:11:49,833
Oh my, Ma'am, don't.

238
00:11:49,967 --> 00:11:51,167
I might lose that.

239
00:11:51,300 --> 00:11:53,833
It's up to you.
That's more suitable for you.

240
00:11:53,967 --> 00:11:55,267
Ma'am, it's up to you.

241
00:11:55,400 --> 00:11:56,067
No. Look at it.

242
00:11:56,200 --> 00:11:57,533
Look at you.

243
00:11:57,667 --> 00:11:58,667
It's up to you.

244
00:11:58,800 --> 00:12:01,033
No, I have a lot
of that in the car.

245
00:12:02,733 --> 00:12:03,567
See?

246
00:12:03,700 --> 00:12:05,167
It fits you perfectly.

247
00:12:07,733 --> 00:12:08,800
Oh my, Miss Yvette...

248
00:12:09,833 --> 00:12:10,467
Thank you.

249
00:12:11,500 --> 00:12:13,333
Because if it weren't for you,

250
00:12:13,467 --> 00:12:16,033
I wouldn't be able
to experience this.

251
00:12:18,867 --> 00:12:22,200
You know, you don't have
to change who you are.

252
00:12:23,333 --> 00:12:27,500
You only have to see yourself
differently sometimes.

253
00:12:31,867 --> 00:12:32,900
Thank you.

254
00:13:26,067 --> 00:13:28,667
Do not cover with your hand
and your bag,

255
00:13:28,967 --> 00:13:30,967
or walk into pitch black.

256
00:13:31,100 --> 00:13:32,667
Then we will lose visuals.

257
00:13:32,800 --> 00:13:34,433
The mic is sensitive.

258
00:13:34,567 --> 00:13:36,400
Keep your hands off it.

259
00:13:36,533 --> 00:13:41,333
And if something goes wrong,
just walk away.

260
00:13:41,467 --> 00:13:42,500
It's okay.

261
00:13:42,633 --> 00:13:44,167
We will still have
footage of the house.

262
00:13:47,967 --> 00:13:49,400
Here's your tactical earpiece.

263
00:13:50,367 --> 00:13:51,367
That's our comms line.

264
00:13:52,067 --> 00:13:52,633
Got it?

265
00:13:56,033 --> 00:13:57,300
You ready?

266
00:13:57,433 --> 00:13:58,100
Yeah.

267
00:13:58,233 --> 00:13:59,133
This is hot.

268
00:13:59,833 --> 00:14:01,300
Well, you wanted that.

269
00:14:01,433 --> 00:14:03,100
You wanted that, remember?

270
00:14:03,233 --> 00:14:05,067
You want to be the one to come.

271
00:14:05,200 --> 00:14:08,500
As for him, he cannot come
because he will be recognized.

272
00:14:08,633 --> 00:14:10,133
I told you I can come with you.

273
00:14:10,267 --> 00:14:11,167
I can be your plus one.

274
00:14:11,300 --> 00:14:12,167
No!

275
00:14:12,300 --> 00:14:13,700
You want to be her plus one?

276
00:14:14,833 --> 00:14:15,733
I'm her best friend.

277
00:14:15,867 --> 00:14:17,633
I will always be her plus one.

278
00:14:17,767 --> 00:14:19,733
And besides, you're Korean.

279
00:14:19,867 --> 00:14:20,700
So what?

280
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:25,300
Yes, you're the one
going with her, right?

281
00:14:29,633 --> 00:14:30,400
Come on, let's go.

282
00:14:37,867 --> 00:14:39,467
Joey, be careful.

283
00:14:41,333 --> 00:14:43,433
I know you are eager
to talk to Golda,

284
00:14:43,567 --> 00:14:49,133
but if it's dangerous, back off.

285
00:14:51,100 --> 00:14:53,433
The important thing is,
you're safe.

286
00:14:54,467 --> 00:14:55,233
Let's go.

287
00:15:51,300 --> 00:15:52,900
Hi, Louise, Louise.

288
00:15:53,033 --> 00:15:53,633
Good to see you.

289
00:15:53,767 --> 00:15:54,733
Thank you for coming.

290
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:57,733
- Hello.
- Happy Birthday.

291
00:15:57,867 --> 00:15:59,167
Thank you, thank you.

292
00:15:59,300 --> 00:16:00,000
Thank you.

293
00:16:00,133 --> 00:16:01,433
Ramon, thank you
for coming, huh?

294
00:16:01,567 --> 00:16:02,933
Thank you for coming.

295
00:16:03,067 --> 00:16:04,400
Thank you, thank you, thank you.

296
00:16:04,533 --> 00:16:07,167
Please, please enjoy yourselves,
enjoy yourselves!

297
00:16:07,300 --> 00:16:08,000
Okay.

298
00:16:10,700 --> 00:16:12,000
There are so many
beautiful ladies today.

299
00:16:22,100 --> 00:16:23,200
Oh, Golda.

300
00:16:23,333 --> 00:16:25,167
Long live the king!

301
00:16:25,300 --> 00:16:27,233
Happy birthday, Godfather.

302
00:16:27,367 --> 00:16:29,867
Thank you, thank you, thank you.

303
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:31,433
Has my gift arrived?

304
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:36,200
I'll call him, Godfather,
and then I'll update you, okay?

305
00:16:37,400 --> 00:16:39,467
But for now, chill!

306
00:16:39,833 --> 00:16:41,567
It's your birthday after all.

307
00:16:41,733 --> 00:16:43,267
Yes.

308
00:16:43,400 --> 00:16:45,267
Enjoy, okay?

309
00:16:45,400 --> 00:16:46,400
I'll see you later.

310
00:17:08,800 --> 00:17:10,400
Dante...

311
00:17:10,533 --> 00:17:11,500
Yes, Godfather?

312
00:17:11,633 --> 00:17:16,133
Secure all entrances
and exits to this place

313
00:17:16,300 --> 00:17:18,267
when Braganza's group arrives.

314
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:20,667
My palm is itching again.

315
00:17:22,433 --> 00:17:23,467
I'm not confident.

316
00:17:24,967 --> 00:17:31,067
If he makes trouble tonight,
make sure no one gets out alive.

317
00:17:31,200 --> 00:17:32,067
Copy, Godfather.

318
00:17:41,700 --> 00:17:42,733
Hey!

319
00:17:42,867 --> 00:17:43,767
- Compadre!
- Hello, Compadre!

320
00:17:43,900 --> 00:17:45,067
How are you?

321
00:17:45,200 --> 00:17:45,867
Happy birthday!

322
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:47,400
Thank you! Thank you for coming!

323
00:17:47,533 --> 00:17:48,567
- Thank you for coming!
- Happy birthday.

324
00:17:48,733 --> 00:17:50,067
Thank you.
I appreciate it.

325
00:17:50,200 --> 00:17:50,867
Hey!

326
00:17:52,400 --> 00:17:54,000
Oh, thank you,
thank you for coming.

327
00:17:54,133 --> 00:17:55,400
Thank you for coming.

328
00:17:56,600 --> 00:17:58,333
Psst, don't smile too much.

329
00:17:58,467 --> 00:17:59,633
Someone might look at you.

330
00:18:01,433 --> 00:18:02,600
You're OA!

331
00:18:09,400 --> 00:18:11,267
Detector.

332
00:18:11,400 --> 00:18:12,500
Psst, don't be loud.

333
00:18:14,333 --> 00:18:15,867
Ah, thank you.

334
00:18:16,733 --> 00:18:18,500
Miss Catalina Esperanza?

335
00:18:20,133 --> 00:18:21,900
Ah, I'm her plus one.

336
00:18:22,067 --> 00:18:22,900
Ah, okay.

337
00:18:23,033 --> 00:18:24,100
<i> You're welcome, plus one.</i>

338
00:18:25,900 --> 00:18:26,567
Thank you. Enjoy the evening.

339
00:18:26,700 --> 00:18:27,300
Thank you.

340
00:18:33,467 --> 00:18:33,933
Wait a minute, Ma'am.

341
00:18:34,067 --> 00:18:34,967
Just SOP.

342
00:18:54,733 --> 00:19:00,400
Sir, don't be loud
because my necklace is fake.

343
00:19:01,800 --> 00:19:03,600
Of course, if it gets lost
inside

344
00:19:03,733 --> 00:19:06,167
and it's real diamonds,
I'll regret it.

345
00:19:06,300 --> 00:19:08,900
So some of the
accessories are fake.

346
00:19:11,100 --> 00:19:11,667
Ah, go ahead.

347
00:19:11,800 --> 00:19:12,700
You can enter now.

348
00:19:20,767 --> 00:19:22,133
Okay.

349
00:19:22,267 --> 00:19:23,133
Thank you.

350
00:19:26,467 --> 00:19:28,333
Joey, I almost had
a heart attack.

351
00:19:34,333 --> 00:19:35,300
Oh my god!

352
00:19:48,400 --> 00:19:50,300
<i> Excuse me, Catalina Esperanza.</i>

353
00:19:52,533 --> 00:19:53,900
Yes, that's me.

354
00:19:54,033 --> 00:19:55,667
Thank God you're here.

355
00:19:55,800 --> 00:19:57,500
The coordinator you were
talking to isn't here.

356
00:19:57,633 --> 00:19:59,300
She just passed on the
instructions about you.

357
00:19:59,433 --> 00:20:00,267
Come with me.

358
00:20:00,400 --> 00:20:03,000
I'll take you to the
performers' area.

359
00:20:03,167 --> 00:20:03,733
What?

360
00:20:03,867 --> 00:20:04,700
Performers?

361
00:20:14,767 --> 00:20:15,533
Let's go.

362
00:20:50,700 --> 00:20:52,033
They have to get out of there
now.

363
00:20:52,167 --> 00:20:53,300
Theresa's here.

364
00:20:53,433 --> 00:20:54,300
Get out of there.

365
00:20:54,433 --> 00:20:55,067
Joey?

366
00:20:55,200 --> 00:20:56,267
Why can't you leave?

367
00:20:56,400 --> 00:20:58,700
This party is so beautiful.

368
00:20:58,833 --> 00:21:02,733
You may not know me,
but I know you very well.

369
00:21:02,867 --> 00:21:04,300
You know, even if I were
the only hope

370
00:21:04,433 --> 00:21:06,300
for Miguel to be released,
I don't want it anymore.

371
00:21:06,433 --> 00:21:08,000
How did someone found out
about our transaction?

372
00:21:08,133 --> 00:21:09,800
You're in my house.

373
00:21:09,967 --> 00:21:12,167
You're not getting
out of here alive.

374
00:21:12,300 --> 00:21:13,367
It's mother!

375
00:21:13,500 --> 00:21:14,500
Get out of the car.

376
00:21:14,633 --> 00:21:15,667
Get out!

377
00:21:15,800 --> 00:21:16,733
Theresa...

378
00:21:16,867 --> 00:21:18,733
I hope your whistleblower
tells you everything.

379
00:21:18,867 --> 00:21:19,733
Who is your source?

380
00:21:19,867 --> 00:21:21,533
We've gotten nothing
out of this mission.

381
00:21:24,033 --> 00:21:24,733
Golda?
